# Example Gemini API Key Backup Pool (.env.backup)
#
# Create a file named `.env.backup` in your workspace root (it is gitignored).
# List your Gemini API keys here (from different Google Cloud/AI Studio accounts
# or backup projects). The rotation script accepts any of the following formats:
#
# Format 1: One key per line (Recommended)
# AIzaSyDxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx1
# AIzaSyDxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx2
# AIzaSyDxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx3
#
# Format 2: Numbered variable assignments
# GEMINI_API_KEY_1=AIzaSyDxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx1
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=AIzaSyDxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx2
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=AIzaSyDxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx3
#
# To rotate to the next key:
#   ./.venv/bin/python scripts/rotate_api_key.py
#
# To test the currently active key:
#   ./.venv/bin/python scripts/rotate_api_key.py --test
#
# To auto-scan the pool and activate the first working, non-exhausted key:
#   ./.venv/bin/python scripts/rotate_api_key.py --auto-find-working
